# Firebase config for the Keeper extension.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values from your own Firebase
# project (Firebase console -> Project settings -> General -> Your apps ->
# SDK setup and configuration). `.env` is gitignored; this template is not.
#
# A note on what these are: none of the values below is a password. A Firebase
# web API key only identifies which project a request belongs to, and it ships
# inside the built extension on every user's machine no matter what you do.
# They live here so you can point the extension at a different Firebase project
# (a scratch one for development, the real one for release) without editing
# code -- not because putting them here hides them.
#
# What actually protects a user's notes is firestore.rules plus Firebase Auth.
#
# The VITE_ prefix is required. Vite only exposes variables starting with VITE_
# to client code; anything else stays out of the bundle.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
